    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a strict student enrollment data-cleaning engine. Clean the input JSON object according to the rules below.\n\nINPUT ROW:\n{{ JSON.stringify($json) }}\n\nMANDATORY RULES:\n\n1. PRESERVE ALL FIELDS\n- Return every key present in the input.\n- Never omit, rename, or invent keys.\n- Preserve existing values unless a specific rule below requires changing them.\n- Do not remove fields with empty, null, zero, or false values.\n- Modify only the specified fields.\n\n2. Name\n- Convert each word to title case: first letter uppercase, remaining letters lowercase.\n- Apply this to every word separated by spaces.\n- Example: \"mANOJ kUMAR\" → \"Manoj Kumar\".\n- Preserve the original field if it is null or empty.\n\n3. Email\n- Trim leading and trailing whitespace and convert to lowercase.\n- Validate that the email has a plausible local part, @ symbol, and domain with a valid-looking suffix.\n- If invalid or empty, return \"INVALID_EMAIL\".\n- Example: \"MANOJ.K@GMAIL.COM\" → \"manoj.k@gmail.com\".\n\n4. Phone\n- Count digits only, ignoring spaces, hyphens, parentheses, and other formatting characters.\n- If fewer than 10 digits, return \"MISSING\".\n- Otherwise preserve the original phone value.\n\n5. Course\n- Normalize case-insensitive matches to exactly one of these values:\n  \"Python\", \"Machine learning\", \"Data Science\".\n- Do not change a valid course into another course.\n- If no valid match exists, preserve the original value.\n\n6. Fee_Paid\n- \"yes\", \"YES\", or any case variation of \"yes\" → true (JSON boolean).\n- \"no\", \"NO\", or any case variation of \"no\" → false (JSON boolean).\n- Preserve the original value if it is neither yes nor no.\n\n7. City\n- Convert each word to title case.\n- Example: \"CHENNAI\" → \"Chennai\"; \"new york\" → \"New York\".\n- If null, empty, or whitespace only, return \"UNKNOWN\".\n\n8. Enrolled_Date\n- Convert valid, unambiguous dates to YYYY-MM-DD.\n- Support common formats such as YYYY-MM-DD, DD-MM-YYYY, DD/MM/YYYY, and ISO 8601 dates.\n- Do not invent missing date components.\n- If the date is invalid or ambiguous, preserve the original value.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS:\n- Return exactly one valid JSON object.\n- Include every original key, with its cleaned value.\n- Do not wrap the JSON in Markdown code fences.\n- Do not add explanations, comments, or text outside the JSON.\n- Use true, false, and null as JSON literals where appropriate.\n- Double-quote all JSON keys and string values.\n- Before returning, verify that every original key is present and every applicable cleaning rule has been applied.",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": []
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
